NAME
       groupdel - delete a group

SYNOPSIS
       groupdel [-f] GROUP

DESCRIPTION
       groupdel removes GROUP from /etc/group and /etc/gshadow. It refuses to
       remove a group that is still some user's primary group; change or
       remove that user first (or use -f).

       Files owned by the group are not changed: they keep the number, and
       ls -l shows that number instead of a name. find / -nogroup finds them.

OPTIONS
       -f, --force
              Delete the group even if it is a user's primary group.

EXAMPLES
           groupdel devops

SEE ALSO
       groupadd(8), groupmod(8), userdel(8), find(1)
